{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:3bb324fbf8fdb85f","name":"Pilot (CL 5)","source":{"id":"source:reference-3bb324fbf8fdb85f","title":"Pilot (CL 5)","revision":18991,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T21:05:56Z","sha256":"367d3c0329123c3dc75d011cecd8737d481acff54b1713e964992f5c32665278","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=18991","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Pilot%20%28CL%205%29&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-3bb324fbf8fdb85f","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Threats of the Galaxy"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Threats_of_the_Galaxy"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Although almost everyone in the civilized portions of the galaxy can drive an ",{"tag":"a","children":["Airspeeder"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Airspeeder"}," or steer a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," through routine routes, pilots are the true experts. The Pilot described here can represent anyone from a fighter pilot, to a ship captain, to a tank commander- as long as a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," needs someone to do some tricky handling, the Pilot is the one to do it. As a result, pilots are in high demand, especially for jobs that involve charting unknown territory or flying through hazardous regions.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Even the most conservative pilot is accustomed to taking risks and knows how to push their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," to the edge if necessary. Many Pilots, especially if they own their own ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},", are also capable mechanics and can lend a hand to ensure that their craft is working at its best. Pilots are skilled at avoiding trouble and keeping their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},", cargo, and passengers safe from harm. \n"]},"\n\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Pilot Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["When not in their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicles"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicles"},", Pilots are typically encountered around hangar bays, barracks, repair shops, or cantinas, relaxing before their next mission. If a pilot is part of a unit of some kind, such as a Rebellion squadron or a planetary militia, they have a rank, which comes with duties and a chain of command, and thus must follow orders. Independent Pilots pursue their own agendas and could be hired for or persuaded to undertake any number of missions. Pilots who man a spaceship commonly call that vessel home. As a result, most Pilots are extremely protective of their ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicle"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicle"}," and are loath to place it in serious risk unless the price is right. Although a pilot might not seem to be much of a threat when not flying their ship, it should be remembered that they can turn the interior of their vessel into a nightmare for intruders- decompressing corridors, turning off the gravity, flooding the engine room with radiation, and the like- all from the safety of the bridge or cockpit.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Pilots are often accompanied by members of their unit or their ship's crew and can call on them for help if things go wrong. Typical allies include the ship's captain, gunner, medic, engineers, or officers (",{"tag":"a","children":["Thugs"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Thugs"}," can be used to represent generic crew). In addition, many Pilots own Astromech Droids that help them by plotting astrogation coordinates or monitoring their ship's internal workings.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Pilot Statistics (CL 5)"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Medium ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nonheroic"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nonheroic","referenceId":"reference:1bca2ef1d9ebe1c3"}," 4/",{"tag":"a","children":["Scout"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Scout","referenceId":"reference:8a1db462be753774"}," 4\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Force Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Force_Points"},":"]}," 2\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Initiative"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Initiative","referenceId":"reference:3e687de48a6ad4e5"},":"]}," +11; ",{"tag":"b","children":["Senses:"]}," ",{"tag":"a","children":["Perception"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Perception","referenceId":"reference:bd18e320a6bb9f53"}," +10\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"b","children":["Languages:"]}," Basic\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Defenses"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Reflex Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Reflex_Defense"},": 17 (",{"tag":"a","children":["Flat-Footed"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Flat-Footed"},": 15), ",{"tag":"a","children":["Fortitude Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Fortitude_Defense"},": 17, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Will Defense"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Will_Defense"},": 15; ",{"tag":"a","children":["Dodge"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Dodge","referenceId":"reference:9444f216899dc20b"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Mobility"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Mobility","referenceId":"reference:e8f000eec8570e3b"},", ",{"tag":"a","children":["Vehicular Combat"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Vehicular_Combat","referenceId":"reference:31246426131b3457"},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Hit Points"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Hit_Points","referenceId":"reference:58e8ee2c9538d027"},": 35, ",{"tag":"a","children":["Damage Threshold"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Damage_Threshold"},": 17\n"]},"\n",{"tag":